    ("continuo_timeline_apply", "POST", "/projects/timeline/apply", "Apply edit verbs by name, atomically, with expected_revision: append, insert, overwrite, split, trim, roll, slip, move, delete, swap_take, set_audio, set_enabled, set_label, add_marker, move_marker, remove_marker, place_music, remove_music, fit_to_beats, put_slot, add_timeline, set_active, rename_timeline, add_audio_track, remove_audio_track, set_track, place_audio, set_gain, set_fades, link_sound, unlink_sound, set_format, set_retime, fit_to_fill, freeze_frame, add_transition, set_transition, remove_transition, set_marker, duplicate_timeline, set_volume_key, remove_volume_key, clear_volume_keys, auto_duck, place_with_parent, lift_range, extract_range, slide, set_speed_curve, add_speed_key, move_speed_key, remove_speed_key, add_hold, snap_speed_key, trim_to_picture, delete_timeline. Frames are integers. Sound tracks A1-A3 (kind audio, role dialogue|music|effects, gain_db, mute, solo, locked) hold sound clips at their own record frames: place_audio {clip:{source:{kind:'media', ref:'file:<sha256>'} from continuo_timeline_audio_add, or kind 'take'}, at_frame, track or role} (a missing role track is made); move (delta, to_track) / trim / roll / slip / split / delete work on them like on V2; set_gain {clip, gain_db} in 0.1 dB steps -60..+24; set_fades {clip, fade_in_frames, fade_out_frames}; set_track {track, role, gain_db, mute, solo, locked}; link_sound {clip, track or role} puts a picture clip's own sound on a sound track, linked (it follows the picture's moves, trims, splits and deletion; unlink_sound frees it). Picture (studio.timeline/1.1): set_format {width, height (even), fit fit|fill|stretch, rate {num,den} only while the cut is empty}; set_retime {clip, percent or speed {num,den} (1..10000 %), reverse, sampling nearest|blend|flow|ai (ai: RIFE in-betweens through the local ComfyUI at export; flow = ffmpeg optical flow)} keeps the clip's source frames and changes its length (100 forward removes it; the clip's own sound stays on only at one speed of 50..200 % forward, pitch-corrected at export; reverse, freeze, ramps and holds turn it off); fit_to_fill {clip, duration_frames}; freeze_frame {clip, at_frame, duration_frames} holds the frame under at_frame on V1; add_transition {left (clip before the V1 cut), kind dissolve|dip_black|dip_white, duration_frames, alignment center|start|end} needs unused media (handles) on both sides and refuses with no_handles; set_transition {id, ...}; remove_transition {id}. set_marker {id, name, note, color} renames a marker; duplicate_timeline {name, source, activate?} copies a cut (new ids) and makes it active unless activate is false. Cuts as items (Media's Cuts group): rename_timeline {timeline, name}; delete_timeline {id} removes a cut (refuses last_cut and cut_in_use; the next cut becomes active); a cut nests into another as ONE clip: append/insert/overwrite with {timeline (the outer cut), clip:{source:{kind:'cut', ref:<inner cut id>}, label, source_in_frame?, duration_frames?}} (media_info and source_rate come from the inner cut; it plays and exports live, keeps its own length, frames past the inner cut's end are black; refuses nest_cycle, nest_rate (another frame rate), nest_empty). Volume automation: a sound clip's volume_keys [{source_frame, gain_db, auto}] sit in its own source frames (they move, trim and split with it), gain_db in 0.1 dB steps added to clip + track gain, linear in dB between keys; set_volume_key {clip, source_frame, gain_db, from_frame?} (a hand key), remove_volume_key {clip, source_frame}, clear_volume_keys {clip or track, auto_only?}. auto_duck {target_role:'music', key_role:'dialogue', depth_db:12, attack_ms:250, release_ms:600, lookahead_ms:250, hold_ms:500} lowers every target-role clip under the speech of every audible key-role sound (all its A tracks + picture clips with sound on) as auto keys, starting lookahead_ms before the first word; speech regions come from the local speech detector (leave speech out) and are cached per file; a re-run replaces only auto keys, hand keys stay; the track keeps the parameters (duck) for the next run. place_with_parent {clip (the parent take's clip on V1), take:{source:{kind:'take', ref:<continuation take id>}}, relation extends|prepends|bridges (the take's mctx.relation), seams {exit, entry} (the frame numbers of the take's mctx.seams: extends exit, prepends entry, bridges both), next (bridges: the clip whose take is seams.entry.source_id)} joins a continuation take to its parent seamlessly in one step: extends cuts the parent at exit and puts the take after it, prepends starts the parent at entry and puts the take before it, bridges cuts the first parent at exit and moves next right after the take, starting at entry; the take keeps the parent's sound setting; answers joins (record frames). Cut over IN-OUT: lift_range {in_frame, out_frame (exclusive: the artist's OUT + 1), tracks? (default every unlocked picture and sound track)} takes those record frames out and leaves a gap (V1 gets one gap, none at the cut's end; clips crossing IN/OUT are cut there; a linked sound goes with its picture); extract_range {same} also closes the hole (ripple: later items move left, free markers too when V1 is chosen); both answer removed, created and range and refuse nothing_in_range. slide {clip (a V1 clip), delta} moves the clip between its neighbours keeping its source and length (the left neighbour's out point and the right one's in point follow, the cut keeps its length), clamped to their handles like roll (requested/applied). trim_to_picture {} ends the song where the last picture clip ends (the same as the music clip menu's Trim song to picture: a song clip crossing that frame loses its tail, one starting after it goes); answers picture_end, trimmed, removed and frames, refuses no_music_lane, no_picture and nothing_to_trim. Speed ramps (a speed curve per picture clip; keys {frame (record frame inside the clip, 0 = its first), percent (0 = hold, 1..10000), ease linear|smooth|step}): set_speed_curve {clip, keys, sampling?} (one key = one speed), add_speed_key {clip, frame, percent? (default: the curve's speed there), ease?}, move_speed_key {clip, frame, to_frame?, percent?, ease?}, remove_speed_key {clip, frame}, add_hold {clip, frame, duration_frames} (the picture stops on that frame for N frames, then goes on), snap_speed_key {clip, frame, grid beat|downbeat|section, map (the placed song's map, as for fit_to_beats; the map comes from continuo_music_map data.map, whose evidence_id continuo_music_open or continuo_music_evidence_import {track_sha256} hands out), every?} puts the key on the nearest event (answers beat). Each keeps the clip's source range, its length follows the speeds (ripple on V1) and answers keys with the source_frame each lands on; a clip with a curve refuses edits that move its first frame (trim its start, split, slide, roll into it: speed_curve), its own sound stays off. Same algebra and revision history as the artist's edits; returns created/removed ids, changed items, placed_refs and the new revision. dry_run=true checks and answers without saving. Send a new request_id (8-64 of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -) with every apply; after a timeout or lost answer retry the same call with the same request_id: if it had landed you get its answer again with replayed=true and nothing is applied twice (same id, other ops: request_id_reused). reason (at most 200 characters) says why; the revision list keeps it. Errors carry code, retryable and next."),
