    ("continuo_timeline_refs", "POST", "/projects/timeline/refs", "List every take and picture any timeline of the project uses (they are in the cut and must stay kept). resolve=true adds media facts and offline marks."),
    ("continuo_timeline_export", "POST", "/projects/timeline/export", "Export one timeline into the project's output folder (a package folder per export; result.folder names it): kind film (exact reference movie, H.264/AAC), fcpxml (FCPXML 1.9 for DaVinci Resolve), fcp7 (FCP7 XML for Premiere Pro), otio (OpenTimelineIO JSON) or edl; each package has EDL, CSVs and video-only media, is verified and fails closed. Pass the document from continuo_timeline_read; its takes, pictures and pinned song resolve from the project by themselves (map sources/music to files in approved folders only to relink). range {in_frame,out_frame} exports only those record frames (the artist's IN-OUT); folder puts the package in a folder inside the approved folders (default the project's output folder). Resolve keeps: FCP7 every cut, the 48 fps take and the markers; FCPXML the cuts (markers via the -markers.edl); OTIO the cuts and markers; EDL one track per file, stills may relink wrongly. The film renders at the cut's format (width, height, fit fit|fill|stretch, rate); retimed clips (speed, reverse, freeze) and V1 transitions (dissolve, dip to black/white) are rendered frame-exactly and written as FCPXML timeMap/transition, FCP7 Time Remap/transitionitem, OTIO LinearTimeWarp/FreezeFrame/Transition and EDL M2/D events, each verified. Speed ramps and holds (retime.curve) are rendered by the one mapping; FCPXML (timeMap) and FCP7 XML (Time Remap graph) carry them exactly; OTIO and EDL carry one speed per clip (one speed or a pure hold exactly, a ramp at its average speed, OTIO with the keys in metadata film_suite.speed_curve) and the package warns per format and clip. Volume keys (auto_duck) are rendered sample-exactly into the film's mix and the music stem (stems sum to the mix) and written as FCPXML adjust-volume keyframes, FCP7 Audio Levels keyframes and OTIO metadata; music_dry=true adds audio/music-dry.wav without them. quality (film): review (H.264/AAC .mp4, default), lossless, or a film master prores_proxy, prores_lt, prores_422, prores_422hq, prores_4444, prores_4444xq (Apple ProRes family, FFmpeg prores_ks), dnxhr_hqx (.mov with PCM 24-bit 48 kHz sound, read back with ffprobe: codec, profile, frame count, durations; result.master). loudness {target_lufs (e.g. -14 online, -23 broadcast; null = no target), ceiling_dbtp (true peak, default -1.0), lra_lu (loudness range EBU R128 LRA in LU, 1-20, default 11; null = Off, the mix keeps its range)} is applied on the mix (or the film's sound) and MEASURED on the written film (result.audio.loudness after: integrated_lufs, true_peak_dbtp); a film above the ceiling fails closed with loudness_over_ceiling. Run continuo_timeline_export_check first. Starts a job in the render queue (continuo_timeline_export_queue); wait_ms (at most 20000 ms) long-polls. subtitles files (default: the cut's subtitle track as <name>.srt and <name>.vtt in every package, FCPXML also as iTT captions) | burn (a film also shows them burned in, the viewer's look) | off; result.subtitles {cues, burned_in, fcpxml_captions, preset}. Never claim Resolve imported it."),
