    ("continuo_timeline_export_cancel", "POST", "/projects/timeline/export/cancel", "Cancel one running or waiting timeline export job; nothing partial is kept."),
    ("continuo_timeline_export_reveal", "POST", "/projects/timeline/export/reveal", "Show a finished timeline export package (job_id) in the artist's file manager: the same as the Deliver sheet's Show in folder."),
    ("continuo_timeline_footage_add", "POST", "/projects/timeline/footage/add", "Make files of the project's own folders (the artist's footage: video or picture, under the approved folders only) usable in the cut: each path is hashed and probed once and answered as ref file:<sha256> with name, frames, rate {num,den}, size, has_audio, codec and vfr (variable frame rate, conformed by frame). Place it with continuo_timeline_apply like a take: clip {source:{kind:'media', ref}, label} (a picture needs duration_frames). Answers never carry a path; a moved or changed file reads offline with its reason."),
    ("continuo_timeline_audio_add", "POST", "/projects/timeline/audio/add", "Make sound files of the project's own folders (wav, mp3, flac, opus, ogg, m4a, aac; approved folders only) usable on the sound tracks A1-A3: each path is hashed, probed and loudness-measured once (ffmpeg ebur128) and answered as ref file:<sha256> with name, samples, sample_rate, channels, duration_seconds, codec and loudness {integrated_lufs, true_peak_dbtp, lra_lu}. With place {expected_revision, role dialogue|music|effects (or track A1-A3), at_frame} it is Add to cut: the files land back to back on that role's sound track (made when the cut has none) in one revision (one undo step). Or place them with continuo_timeline_apply place_audio {clip:{source:{kind:'media', ref}}, at_frame, role}. Answers never carry a path; a moved or changed file reads offline with its reason."),
    ("continuo_timeline_peaks", "POST", "/projects/timeline/peaks", "Read the waveform of one sound source the cut uses (a sound file ref file:<sha256>, a take's own sound studio:..., or the pinned song by its sha256): min/max peaks per bucket at buckets_per_second (1..1000), decoded samples, sample_rate, channels and the registered loudness. sound=true adds the sound as lossless FLAC (base64) for the Timeline's preview mix. Read-only; answers never carry a path; an offline source or one without sound answers source_offline / no_sound."),
    ("continuo_h3_sound_check", "POST", "/generation/sound/check", "Check the sound of a local MiniMax H3 Frames/References request before submitting (target_id, args with duration_seconds and the sound fields as for continuo_video_submit, approved_roots): per file its length, the part used and its <Audio N>; total_seconds of the voice/music references against limit_seconds 15; problem names why a submit would refuse it. Reads only; nothing is uploaded or generated."),
    ("continuo_take_lineage", "POST", "/generation/take/lineage", "Read one finished local H3 take's continuation facts (owner_scope, studio_job_id): continuable, offers (extend, prepend, bridge) or the plain reason it offers nothing (a take made before continuation existed), mctx {self_id, parent_id, parents, relation extends|prepends|bridges|root, pins, delivered_frames, seams exit/entry frames}, its parents and children in the scope and the relation label (continues, leads into, bridges). Use it before submitting minimax-h3-extend-mctx-v1 / -prepend-mctx-v1 / -bridge-mctx-v1 with continuo_video_submit (args source = the take's file, bridge also target = a second continuable take of the same picture size). Read-only."),
    ("continuo_media_peaks", "POST", "/media/peaks", "Read the waveform of one sound file in artist-approved roots (path, approved_roots) or of one finished generated sound of the scope (owner_scope, studio_job_id): min/max peaks per bucket over every channel (buckets 8-400), samples, sample_rate, channels and duration_seconds; read-only, never a path in the answer. The same peaks Media draws on a sound tile."),
    # Script (lane script): the project's screenplay studio.script/1, one tool per hand action.
    ("continuo_script_read", "POST", "/projects/script/read", "Read the project's screenplay and its revision. view=fountain gives the whole script as Fountain with a [[s-xxxxxxxx]] note before each scene and [[a-xxxxxxxx]] before each act break (aside scenes in a /* */ at the end); structured gives scenes {text, synopsis, card, number, omitted, revision, by} and order. derived lists scene numbers, aside ids, characters and places, acts [{title, first_scene}] (the author's centered act marks such as > AKT 1 <) and act_end {title, after_scene} | null (read-only)."),
    ("continuo_script_revisions", "POST", "/projects/script/revisions", "List kept script revisions (label, author, time), or read one with revision=N."),
    ("continuo_script_scene_add", "POST", "/projects/script/scene/add", "Add one scene: text is Fountain (heading first line, no #number#, no [[id]]), optional synopsis, at {index | before: id | after: id} (default end), aside=true keeps it out of the order. Answers the new scene id."),
    ("continuo_script_scene_write", "POST", "/projects/script/scene/write", "Replace one scene's text and/or synopsis. A scene changed after expected_revision answers 409 scene_conflict with current and proposed; nothing is saved. Other scenes never conflict."),
    ("continuo_script_scene_omit", "POST", "/projects/script/scene/omit", "Omit a scene (omitted=false restores it): it keeps its place and number and exports as OMITTED."),
    ("continuo_script_scene_delete", "POST", "/projects/script/scene/delete", "Delete a scene. A scene that ever had a locked number is refused (scene_numbered): omit it instead; force=true only when the artist asks."),
    ("continuo_script_move", "POST", "/projects/script/move", "Move scenes and/or act breaks (items: ids) to at {index | before: id | after: id}; several keep their order in the script. Never touches text."),
    ("continuo_script_aside", "POST", "/projects/script/aside", "Take scenes out of the order (aside=true; they stay in the document) or put aside scenes back (aside=false, at)."),
    ("continuo_script_break_add", "POST", "/projects/script/break/add", "Add an act break with a title at {index | before: id | after: id}."),
    ("continuo_script_break_rename", "POST", "/projects/script/break/rename", "Rename an act break (break: its id)."),
    ("continuo_script_break_remove", "POST", "/projects/script/break/remove", "Remove an act break; its scenes stay."),
    ("continuo_script_card_place", "POST", "/projects/script/card/place", "Place a scene's card at x, y on the board (clear=true removes the position). Has its own revision; never conflicts with text edits."),
    ("continuo_script_numbers", "POST", "/projects/script/numbers", "Lock (locked=true) or unlock scene numbers. While locked, numbers stay and a scene put between 12 and 13 gets 12A."),
    ("continuo_script_title_page", "POST", "/projects/script/title-page", "Replace the title page: entries [{key, value}] (Title, Credit, Author, Draft date, Contact...)."),
    ("continuo_script_write", "POST", "/projects/script/write", "Write the whole script back as Fountain from continuo_script_read view=fountain. Scenes map by their [[s-...]] note; a scene without a known note is new (answered in created); a scene left out is set aside (set_aside), never deleted; # lines are act breaks. Each changed scene conflicts like scene_write; all or nothing."),
    ("continuo_script_import", "POST", "/projects/script/import", "Import a Fountain or FDX screenplay (format, text) as the project's script; replaces it, so pass the current revision (0 when none). Fountain # sections become act breaks, /* */ scenes aside, #12A# and FDX Number locked numbers, FDX SceneProperties Title/Summary the synopsis. Answers what was not kept."),
    ("continuo_script_export", "POST", "/projects/script/export", "Export the script as Fountain, FDX or PDF into the project's exports/script folder (name-r<revision>.<format>). Aside scenes are not in FDX. PDF is Courier 12 on US Letter laid out by the same page rules as derived.pages (answers pages = derived.pages.total; a title page comes first when the script has one). Answers the relative file."),
    # Script History (lane w10-script item 3): Undo/Restore of a kept revision, as the page's History tab does.
    ("continuo_script_restore", "POST", "/projects/script/restore", "Bring a kept script revision back as a new revision (revision = N from continuo_script_revisions, expected_revision = the current revision); the page's History Undo does the same. Answers the new revision. Only when the artist asks."),
    # Lane p5-scr: the script's page size (US Letter / A4), charter decision 4.
    ("continuo_script_page_size", "POST", "/projects/script/page-size", "Set the page size of the script: size letter (US Letter, default) or a4. Editor, PDF and derived.pages break on the same lines for that size; derived.pages.size names it."),
    ("continuo_image_edits_read", "POST", "/image/edits/read", "Read the Image edits kept with an owner scope (a project keeps them in its folder): with sha256s (up to 16 Originals, the sha256 Edit > Info shows) each picture's develop values (masks, crop and layers included), its packed History (studio.image-history/1: rows and position) and its revision; without sha256s the list of pictures that have edits. The same values the Edit pane opens the picture with."),
    ("continuo_image_edits_write", "POST", "/image/edits/write", "Keep one picture's develop values and packed History (sha256 of the Original, expected_revision 0 when it has none yet). Another revision answers 409 with the current one and changes nothing; over 512 KB per picture, 5000 pictures or 256 MB per scope it refuses and removes nothing. The pane reads it when the picture is next opened; to change the picture open in Edit use continuo_image_action."),
    # Image output (lane w1-imgout): SeedVR2 upscale, picture export with the recipe in the file, restore by drop.
    ("continuo_image_upscale", "POST", "/image/upscale", "Upscale an owned picture (source image_producer_job_id or kept revision_id) with the local SeedVR2 7B: factor 2 or 4, or long_edge (even, larger than the picture's, at most 8192); tile_size, tile_overlap and color_correction from continuo_image_upscale_capabilities. The result is a NEW picture of the same work (the Original is never changed); poll it with continuo_image_poll, keep it with continuo_image_keep. Stable operation_id; a replay renders nothing twice. Only on the artist's request."),
    ("continuo_image_upscale_capabilities", "GET", "/image/upscale/capabilities", "Read what Upscale offers (factors, long edge bounds, tile size/overlap and colour correction options with defaults) and whether the image engine has SeedVR2 and its files now; never runs a job."),
    ("continuo_image_export", "POST", "/image/export", "Export an owned picture or kept version (source image_producer_job_id or revision_id) as a file into the project's exports/images folder: format png (bit_depth 8|16), jpeg (quality 1-100), webp (quality, or lossless), tiff (bit_depth 8|16); size {mode original | long_edge value | percent value}; sRGB profile embedded (display_p3 is refused with the reason); metadata=true embeds the Suite recipe studio.image-recipe/1 (model, prompt, seed, settings, parent sha256), false writes none. No project is refused. Never replaces a file; answers the relative file, size, bit depth and recipe."),
    ("continuo_image_export_options", "GET", "/image/export/options", "Read the export formats, bit depths, quality, size modes, colour profiles (with the reason one is unavailable) and where the recipe goes in each format."),
    ("continuo_image_recipe_read", "POST", "/image/recipe/read", "Read the Suite recipe (studio.image-recipe/1) a dropped picture carries: data_b64 bytes, or path inside approved_roots the artist approved. found=false with reason no_recipe for a picture without one. recipe.apply holds the route and settings the page uses for Use these settings; apply them only on the artist's request."),
    # Continuo frame (lane w1-frame): the bar's GPU line, read-only.
    ("continuo_gpu_status", "GET", "/system/gpu", "Read the GPU memory line the Jobs popover shows: per GPU name, memory_used_mb and memory_total_mb (nvidia-smi, cached 2 s); available=false when there is no GPU or no nvidia-smi. Read-only."),
    ("continuo_music_open", "POST", "/music/open", "Open a song of the artist's approved folders the way the Audio page does, without analysing it: length, waveform peaks, the playback proxy, track_sha256, analysed (true when an earlier analysis of this file content is stored, then its result in analysis), the beat engines (Beat This! the default when installed, librosa the basic fallback) and default_engine; with an analysis also evidence_id and map_id (the song map continuo_music_map / continuo_use_in_cut use; null when unreadable). Never computes beats or sections."),
    ("continuo_music_analyse_start", "POST", "/music/analyse/start", "Start the song analysis (beats, meter, bar 1, sections, key) on request, as the Audio page's Analyse button does; it costs compute, so run it only when beats are needed (e.g. before cutting on the beat). engine beat_this (default when installed) or librosa. A song on a Cut music lane is named by track_sha256 + project_ref instead of path (the Cut starts this itself, once per file). Returns job_id at once; a stored result for this file content is reused without analysing again. Poll continuo_music_analyse_status; continuo_music_analyse_stop stops it."),
    ("continuo_music_analyse_status", "POST", "/music/analyse/status", "Read one song analysis job: status running|done|stopped|error, progress 0-1, stage, and on done the analysis (the same result the Audio page shows)."),
    ("continuo_music_analyse_stop", "POST", "/music/analyse/stop", "Stop a running song analysis (the Audio page's Stop); nothing is stored. Answers the job's status."),
    # lane p12-int (route of p12-aud AUD-010): read the stored IN-OUT; the Audio page is its only writer.
    ("continuo_music_range_read", "POST", "/music/range/read", "Read the stored IN-OUT of one song (track_sha256) in the project: range {start, end} in seconds, null when the whole song is in use, and by (artist or hermes), who set it. To set IN-OUT use continuo_music_action set_selection; the Audio page stores it."),
    ("continuo_control_extract", "POST", "/media/control/extract", "Make control layers of one clip or picture of the scope, as Media does on Extract: layers any of pose, depth, edges, lineart, camera; the source is a take or picture by source_id (studio:... / imgjob_...) or a file of artist-approved roots (path, approved_roots); range_in/range_out in seconds (at most 60 s). Runs locally only (ComfyUI on this PC for pose/depth/edges, CPU for line art and camera move), cached per content; answers a job (wait_ms up to 20000) whose items are the new Media layers grouped under their source. Never cancels anything in ComfyUI."),
    ("continuo_control_status", "POST", "/media/control/status", "Read one control-layer extraction job (job_id, wait_ms long-poll): state, the layer running, the layers done as Media items, and a plain sentence for every layer that could not be made (no person found, model missing, ComfyUI not running)."),
    ("continuo_control_stop", "POST", "/media/control/stop", "Stop a control-layer extraction after the layer running now, like Stop in Media; the running ComfyUI prompt is never cancelled. Only when the artist asks."),
    ("continuo_control_list", "POST", "/media/control/list", "List the control layers of the scope (or of one source: derived_from) grouped under their source, as Media shows them: item_id, layer, kind (video, image or text), derived_from, the camera sentence for a camera layer, and the layer file."),
    ("continuo_control_use", "POST", "/media/control/use", "The hand-off of one control layer, the same as Media's buttons: use motion_guide (a pose/depth/edges/line-art clip for the Motion guide of a References video model: path + the folder to approve), camera (the camera sentence for the camera part of a video prompt) or image_control (a layer picture for Image). Read-only: it tells where the layer goes; placing it is a Video/Image state change."),
    ("continuo_take_freeze_check", "POST", "/generation/take/freeze-check", "Read one finished local H3 take's freeze verdict (owner_scope, studio_job_id): verdict frozen/moving/unmeasured, global and local frame-to-frame change, and hold_end (last vs first frame). Measured once when published; a frozen take is marked, never hidden. Little motion: check the take."),
    ("continuo_take_finish", "POST", "/generation/take/finish", "Finish one finished local MiniMax H3 take into a NEW take (explicitly authorized, uses the local GPU): client_request_id, studio_job_id of the source take, upscale (latent upscale lbh to 1.5 MP, multiple of 32; default on) and rife (RIFE 48 fps; default off), at least one on, plus save_to/requested_basename/approved_roots like continuo_video_submit. The take needs its continuation sidecar; the source stays untouched. Poll the answer's details.id with continuo_video_poll; its take facts carry finish {source, source_job, upscale, rife, fps, frames, canvas}. Temporal 2x/3x is not offered."),
    ("continuo_voice_state_read", "POST", "/voice/state/read", "Read the project's voices (clip ref + IN/OUT + words, or description, seed), characters -> voice, lines (character, text with {cue:sigh}, direction) and the Audio page's take choices, with the revision to write against."),
    ("continuo_voice_state_write", "POST", "/voice/state/write", "Save voices, characters, lines and take choices whole with expected_revision; preserve what you did not change. Never invent a clip's words: leave them empty or use continuo_voice_transcribe."),
    ("continuo_voice_import", "POST", "/voice/import", "Copy sound files of an artist-chosen folder (paths inside source_roots) into the project (<first approved folder>/Voice/References) and make each a voice; transcribe=true writes their words with the local recognizer. Only when the artist asks."),
    ("continuo_voice_transcribe", "POST", "/voice/transcribe", "Write the words of one voice's clip (its IN-OUT) with the local recognizer (CPU, no download). Answers words null when none could be read."),
    ("continuo_voice_targets", "POST", "/voice/targets", "List the local voice targets: engine, voice source (clip or description), whether words are required, cues, the controls each really has (section delivery/pauses/performance) and readiness with reasons. check=false skips the engine."),
    ("continuo_voice_generate", "POST", "/voice/generate", "Speak one line N times (count 1-8) on a local voice target with explicit artist intent: one take per seed (seeds, or seed, seed+1, ...). Answers the take ids at once; takes run one after another behind anything already in the engine's queue. Read progress with continuo_voice_takes. Pass request_id (8-64 of A-Za-z0-9_-, new per batch): a retry with the same id and request answers the same batch (replayed true), another request under it is refused request_id_reused."),
    ("continuo_voice_takes", "POST", "/voice/takes", "List the takes of one line (line_id) or all: state waiting/running/ready/failed, progress 0-1, seconds, loudness {integrated_lufs, true_peak_dbtp}, gain_db, selected, kept, rating, seed, target, the time it took and the failure reason. Kept and rating are Media marks (continuo_media_marks_write with item_id = studio_job_id)."),
    ("continuo_voice_take_set", "POST", "/voice/take/set", "Select a take for its line (one per line) and/or set its gain_db (-24..+24, non-destructive)."),
    ("continuo_voice_match", "POST", "/voice/match", "Match level: give the line's finished takes a gain each so they sit at one loudness (their median, or target_lufs); reset=true sets every gain back to 0. Files never change."),
    ("continuo_voice_take_sound", "POST", "/voice/take/sound", "One finished take as FLAC (base64) with its gain applied, for listening; never a path."),
    ("continuo_voice_take_to_cut", "POST", "/voice/take/to-cut", "Add a finished take to the cut: on the Dialogue sound track (or role music/effects) at at_frame with its gain, labelled with the line, in one timeline revision (expected_revision of the timeline)."),
    ("continuo_timeline_export_check", "POST", "/projects/timeline/export/check", "Check before render, the same as Deliver's Check before render: pass the document (and range / sources / music exactly as for continuo_timeline_export); nothing renders. Answers ok, blocking, warnings and items [{code, severity block|warn, clips (ids), fix, message, hint}]: offline (block: picture clips, sound clips or the song lane whose file is gone; fix locate = relink), offline_outside (warn: offline clips outside the range; the range renders, the entire timeline does not), invalid (block: the export would refuse the cut), rate_mismatch (warn: moving sources at another rate than the cut, e.g. 48 fps takes on a 24 fps cut, with their source_rate), variable_rate (warn: phone clips conformed by frame). Render only when ok is true."),
    ("continuo_timeline_export_queue", "POST", "/projects/timeline/export/queue", "The render queue, the same as Deliver's queue: action list (default) answers every export job of the project in order (number, state waiting/running/done/failed/cancelled, position for waiting jobs, progress, stage, label, result or error), running and waiting; one renders at a time, the rest wait their turn in order. action remove + job_id takes a waiting job out (it never runs; a running one is cancelled with continuo_timeline_export_cancel); action clear_finished drops done, failed and cancelled jobs from the list (their packages stay on disk). The queue is stored in the project and survives a restart: each row has its settings; a job that was rendering when the app closed is failed with app_closed; action again + job_id renders a finished job's stored request as a new job."),
    ("continuo_h3_controls", "POST", "/generation/h3/controls", "Read the local MiniMax H3 Frames/References inspector controls (body {} or {target_id}): per control its section (sampling, loras, performance), options, default, live state available|unavailable (with the reason, e.g. the engine lacks the node) and proof rendered|untested, the MiniMax H3 LoRA files the engine lists, and count 1-8. Send them as extra args of continuo_video_submit on minimax-h3-frames-v1 / -references-v1: turbo (bool, default true), turbo_strength 0-2 (0.8), recipe native|sandwich|fast_0903 (sandwich/fast_0903 need >= 7 steps; fast_0903 delivers twice the size), sigma_shift_video (12) / sigma_shift_audio (3), engine native|shark, loras [{file, strength 0-2}] (MiniMax H3 LoRAs the engine lists, max 8), attention comfy_kitchen|sage|pytorch, sparse off|sla|native with sparsity (sla 0.6-0.95, native = sol-attn tau 0-4), cache none|t8|spectrum, count 1-8 (N takes with seed + i and one batch id; the answer's batch.takes lists them, later takes start as the previous one ends, retry the same client_request_id to read them). Leave a control out to keep the pinned graph; an unavailable option is refused before anything is queued. Read-only."),
    # Image Box (lane w2-imgbox): boxes with an intent go through continuo_image_edit (operation "box"); Find and the final prompt.
    ("continuo_image_box_find", "POST", "/image/box/find", "Find boxes on an owned picture (source image_producer_job_id or revision_id) for a text query (\"lighthouse\"), like Image Box Find...: the local SAM3 detector answers boxes {id, label, score, bbox [x, y, w, h] in picture pixels}, highest score first, ids numbered left to right (lighthouse_1 ...). threshold 0.05-0.95 (default 0.4), max_boxes 1-16; wait_ms long-polls up to 20000. Same picture + query is one job. Use the boxes in continuo_image_edit with operation box and an intent per box; finding never edits."),
    ("continuo_image_box_prompt", "POST", "/image/box/prompt", "Read what a box edit would send without running it (the Final prompt of Image Box): width/height of the picture, prompt, boxes [{id, intent add|change|move|keep|remove, desc, bbox [x, y, w, h], target_bbox for move}], model {family}. FLUX.3 Klein (default): final_prompt (caption + one sentence per box the prompt does not name as <id> + BFL list on the crop) and the crop; other edit models: the Fill/Replace/Remove the boxes become and the mask facts, or the reason Move is refused."),
    # Audio page stems (lane w3-audio): separate a sound file on the local engine with installed node packs only.
    ("continuo_audio_stems_start", "POST", "/audio/stems/start", "Separate one sound file of the approved folders into stems on the local ComfyUI, as the Audio page's Separate stems does: path, approved_roots, split vocals_rest (Mel-Band RoFormer: vocals + rest) or four (HDEMUCS: vocals, drums, bass, other). Only with the artist's ask; it uses the GPU behind whatever is queued. Stored stems of the same file and split answer status done at once (job_id null). Poll continuo_audio_stems_status; continuo_audio_stems_stop stops waiting (never cancels the engine)."),
    ("continuo_audio_stems_status", "POST", "/audio/stems/status", "Read one stems job: status running|done|stopped|error, progress 0-1, stage, and on done the result {split, sample_rate, seconds, stems [{id, label, seconds, peaks}], measured {lengths_equal, residual_db (mix minus the sum of the stems, dB below the mix)}}."),
    ("continuo_audio_stems_stop", "POST", "/audio/stems/stop", "Stop waiting for a stems job (the Audio page's Stop); the engine finishes on its own, nothing is kept."),
    ("continuo_audio_stems_read", "POST", "/audio/stems/read", "The stored stems of a sound file for a split (result null when not separated yet) and whether each split can run on this machine (splits {vocals_rest, four}: ready + reasons). Reads only."),
    ("continuo_audio_stems_sound", "POST", "/audio/stems/sound", "The audible stems summed (audible: stem ids, the Audio page's Solo / Mute) as FLAC base64 for listening; never a path."),
    ("continuo_audio_stems_to_media", "POST", "/audio/stems/to-media", "Add stems to Media (the Audio page's Add stems to Media): copies the stored stems (all, or stems: ids) into the project's first approved folder under Stems/<song>/, where Media lists them as sound files with their file:<sha256> ids."),
    ("continuo_voice_take_import", "POST", "/voice/take/import", "Make a recording a take of a line (line_id): a sound file inside source_roots (an artist-chosen folder) is copied into the line's Voice folder and published as a take with its sha256, length and loudness; Media lists it. The Audio page's drop zone does the same. Only when the artist asks."),
    ("continuo_voice_take_words", "POST", "/voice/take/words", "Read the words of one finished take with their start/end seconds (local recognizer on the CPU, no download) and keep them on the take; continuo_voice_takes then carries words [{w, start, end}] (the Audio page's words lane). Answers words null when nothing could be read."),
    ("continuo_voice_take_recut", "POST", "/voice/take/recut", "Re-cut pauses (no re-speaking): set the pauses between a finished take's words (it needs word timings, continuo_voice_take_words first): gaps {word index: seconds} for the pause after that word, max_pause shortens every longer pause, end_pause the sound after the last word. Cuts in the middle of each pause (no word is touched) and publishes a NEW take of the line (recut_of names the source, which stays). Only when the artist asks."),
    ("continuo_voice_history_read", "POST", "/voice/history/read", "The Audio page's History of this project, newest first: entries {by artist|hermes, text, at}."),
    ("continuo_voice_history_add", "POST", "/voice/history/add", "Add one line to the Audio page's History (by hermes for what you did on the artist's ask); kept with the project."),
    # Take A/B review (lane w5-review): the Video page Take tab's Compare A|B, one clock; decisions append-only per project.
    ("continuo_review_start", "POST", "/projects/review/start", "Start an A/B comparison of two finished takes of one shot, the same as the Take tab's Compare: takes [{id (studio job id), label}] (or {id, path} inside the approved folders), shot (the Script shot id sh-xxxxxxxx when the takes came from a Script shot, otherwise the take's own id), blind (labels hidden and the order shuffled until a choice), by hermes. Answers the comparison (comparison_id, slot a and b with take id and sha256 of the file); the open page shows it. Never decide for the artist."),
    ("continuo_review_read", "POST", "/projects/review/read", "Read the project's A/B comparisons (optionally of one shot), newest first, with their frame notes and decision, the open ones, and every decision {take_ids, sha256, blind, chosen, chosen_sha256, notes, by, at}."),
    ("continuo_review_note", "POST", "/projects/review/note", "Add a note to one frame of a comparison (comparison_id, frame, text, by hermes); it shows as a mark on the shot's track and is stored with the decision."),
    ("continuo_review_decide", "POST", "/projects/review/decide", "Store Prefer A or B for a comparison (chosen a|b, by). Only when the artist said which take they prefer; a comparison is decided once."),
